  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wood Solution Thailand Engagement Phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Wood Solution Thailand Engagement Phase (March-June 2026), co-financed by Sida and the Royal Thai Embassy, was designed as a preparatory phase for a larger, multi-year effort to support Thailand in developing a competitive, sustainable, and inclusive wood-production and timber-construction industrial system. The engagement phase of the program aims to:
&#x2022; support pioneer initiatives across the full value chain &#x2013; from forestry to construction &#x2013; demonstrating practical wood-based solutions.
&#x2022; develop the Wood Solution Support Platform, an international network of experts and technology providers supporting the entire value chain from forestry to timber construction.
&#x2022; build funding partnerships with bilateral, multilateral, philanthropic, and private-sector actors for the next phase.
&#x2022; align with the Thailand-Sweden Strategic Partnership (August 2025), fostering business-to-business collaboration between Thai and Swedish actors.</narrative>
  </description>
